  "worked_solution": "First, we must find the elements of the sets $A$ and $B.$\n\n- The elements of the set $A$ are all positive integers that satisfy the inequality $x\\le 3.$ So, we have \n\n$$\nA={1,2,3}.\n$$\n\n- On the other hand, the elements of the set $B$ are all integers that satisfy the inequality $0\\le x<3.$ So, we have\n\n$$\nB={0,1,2}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's inspect the given statements.\n\n- $A\u2286B$ is false. For example, $3\\in A$ but $3\\notin B.$\n\n- $B\u2288A$ is true. For example, $0\\in B$ but $0\\notin A.$\n\n- $\u2205\u2288B$ is false. The null set $\u2205={}$ is a subset of *every* set.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"",
